  "lawGradeScale": "v4 law grading scale (native canon scale, strongest first): DERIVED, LOCKED, MAPPED, PARTIAL, SPLIT, OPEN, DEFINITIONAL. Mapping to C0-C6 unruled - tracked as OI-0011.",
  "statementTechnical": "Two halves. Shannon half: channel capacity C = B log2(1 + S/N) - well-defined, quantifiable, Lean-formalizable; capacity maps to the channel through which Logos communicates. Kolmogorov half: irreducible complexity maps to the content of divine speech - meaning is not Shannon information. Logos (John 1:1) is claimed as both channel and message. Canonical grade SPLIT: the Shannon half is strong and formalizable; the Kolmogorov half carries the theological weight and is the weaker leg.",
  "statementPlain": "Shannon told us how to measure what a channel can carry; Kolmogorov told us some content cannot be compressed. The proposal: the Word is both the channel and the message - and the meaning of the message is precisely the part information rate cannot measure. The Shannon half of this law is strong and formalizable; the Kolmogorov half is where the theology lives, and it remains open - if meaning ever collapses into mere information rate, this law's own kill condition says it fails.",
  "mathematicalForm": "C = B log2(1 + S/N); K(x) = min{|p| : U(p) = x}; claim: meaning not reducible to Shannon rate",
  "mathFormNormal": "C = B log2(1 + S/N); K(x) = min{|p| : U(p) = x}; claim: meaning not reducible to Shannon rate",
